      "message": "I\u0027m actually not sure we should provide a public getNextKey method that accepts a null key. Is such a method useful? If not, we can maybe do:\n\n    private K getNextKeyInternal(@Nullable K key) throws ErrnoException {\n        final byte[] rawKey \u003d getNextRawKey(\n                key \u003d\u003d null ? null : key.writeToBytes());\n        ...\n        ...\n    }\n\n    @Nullable\n    public K getNextKey(@NonNull K key) throws ErrnoException {\n        Objects.requireNonNull(key);\n        return getNextKeyInternal(key);\n    }\n\n    @Nullable\n    private K getFirstKey() throws ErrnoException {\n        return getNextKeyInternal(null);\n    }",
