      "side": 1,
      "message": "Make public getNextKey method doesn\u0027t accept a null key. getNextKeyInternal() is used by public getFirstKey() and public forEach() now.\n\nCurrent getNextKey() looks likes that implements as what BPF_MAP_GET_NEXT_KEY does. Null key is allowed by kernel. Per discussed with Mark, probably making public getNextKey not allow null key makes the design easier and leave null key for getFirstKey() internal use only \n\nhttps://github.com/iovisor/bcc/blob/master/src/cc/libbpf.c#L363\nint bpf_get_first_key(int fd, void *key, size_t key_size)\n   // 4.12 and above kernel supports passing NULL to BPF_MAP_GET_NEXT_KEY\n   // to get first key of the map. For older kernels, the call will fail.\n   res \u003d bpf_map_get_next_key(fd, 0, key);\n\n\n\nBy the way, forEach also need to use getNextKeyInternal because it uses getNextKey(null) to start iterating on the first entry.\n\nL.185\n    public void forEach(BiConsumer\u003cK, V\u003e action) throws ErrnoException {\n        K curKey \u003d null;\n..\n        while ((nextKey \u003d getNextKey(curKey)) !\u003d null) {\n\n\nLeave this as unresolved if need more discussion",
