      "message": "Having tried this before, I think the answer is: no, you can\u0027t.\n\nInet6Address is a subclass of InetAddress, and it doesn\u0027t override getByAddress. So Inet6Address.getByAddress behaves exactly the same as InetAddress.getByAddress. As such, Inet6Address.getByAddress({new byte[]{1, 2, 3, 4}) will happily return an IPv4 address without throwing any exceptions.\n\nThat said - if you have a test that demonstrates that this works, then yes you can. :-)",
